      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Steam frame is arm64, and uses emulation to run x86/x64 code. \n\nI'm curious to see how things go. But I suspect that how vrchat works on PC might work contrary to how the emulation stuff can work. Like with a set video game if there are a few shaders that need tweaking, they can either replace or ask a dev to replace or tweak. But every vrchat world can have its own quirky shaders. \n\n16gb of RAM with the hardware it has they could easily run the Android version and not run out of RAM very easily. \n\nWe'll have to see what vrchat is able to get out of the Steam frame, I know they'll try everything but I suspect they'll spare us the details.",
